# `lint-staged`, not `npx lint-staged`. `_/h` puts `node_modules/.bin` on PATH, so the
# bare command resolves with no registry round trip. `npx` in a tree with no install
# fetches the package instead: 70 seconds before failing when the registry is
# unreachable, and a silent download when it is not.
#
# The preflight names every command this hook shells out to, the two behind `npm run`
# included — a missing `tsc` is reported by npm's inner shell, which husky never sees, so
# that one arrives as `code 127` with no husky line at all. The list lives here rather
# than inside the script so it stays on the line above the body it answers for.
sh scripts/hook-requires.sh pre-commit lint-staged tsc vitest
lint-staged
npm run tsc
npm run test
